<title>USA: Sprint launches &quot;private&quot; Internet link.</title>
<headline>Sprint launches &quot;private&quot; Internet link.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sprint Corp said Monday it launched its Internet Private Passport to provide Internet access to specific groups of users.</p>
<p>Sprint said initial customers for the product include Viacom Inc units Macmillan Publishing and Simon &amp; Schuster Interactive, and the California Medical Association.</p>
<p>The Internet Private Passport allows key products and services in its primary Internet service to be customized for specific communities, organizations and products.</p>
<p>The customization gives users a private gateway to the organizations' content and applications, along with general access to the Internet.</p>
<p>((--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
